error[E0277]: `Cons<Cons<A, Cons<B, notko_hlist::Empty>>, notko_hlist::Empty>` does not hold `A`
  --> tests/compile_fail/membership_does_not_descend_into_a_head.rs:17:13
   |
17 |     holds::<Nested, A>();
   |             ^^^^^^ the trait `Contains<A>` is not implemented for `Cons<Cons<A, Cons<B, notko_hlist::Empty>>, notko_hlist::Empty>`
   |
   = note: Membership is decided by walking the cells, so `Cons<Cons<A, Cons<B, notko_hlist::Empty>>, notko_hlist::Empty>` has to be a list built from `Empty` and `Cons<H, T>`, and `A` has to be one of its heads. If the compiler reports `overflow evaluating the requirement` instead, the list is deeper than the default recursion limit and the crate root wants `#![recursion_limit = "1024"]`.
note: required by a bound in `holds`
  --> tests/compile_fail/membership_does_not_descend_into_a_head.rs:14:13
   |
14 | fn holds<L: Contains<X>, X>() {}
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `holds`
